# Scholaracle Scraper Library — AI Coding Rules

ROLE: engineer STRICT=true

## Stack
TypeScript 5.3 strict | Node 20 | Jest 29 | Playwright | Commander

## Always apply
- Search codebase first; reuse patterns; follow `src/scrapers/_template/` for new scrapers
- TDD (M1): failing test first for features/bug fixes
- Three-file scrapers (M3): metadata.json + scraper + transformer
- Types from `src/core/types.ts` (M8); TransformContext for keys (M4)
- Extend BaseScraper lifecycle (M6); validate envelope before upload (M5)
- No credentials in code/logs; no real browsers/portals/APIs in tests (M7)
- Strict TS: no `any` (except immediate cast of `page.evaluate`); throw errors; no console.log

## Full mandates
When editing scrapers/transformers/bin: load `.cursor/rules/scraper-mandates.mdc` (M1–M9, envelope, E2E).

## Quick cmds
`npm test` | `npm run type-check` | `npm run lint` | `npx scholaracle-scraper validate <platform>`
